WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.306 --> 00:00:03.203
- [Announcer] Vladimir
Vladimirovich Putin.

00:00:04.044 --> 00:00:05.040
- [Narrator] For more than two decades,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.000
the Russian president

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.855
has been cultivating a strong man image.

00:00:08.855 --> 00:00:09.688
(man falling)

00:00:09.688 --> 00:00:10.521
He's a judo master

00:00:10.521 --> 00:00:13.740
who rides horses, swims
in a Siberian river

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.965
and scores goals in hockey
against world champions.

00:00:16.965 --> 00:00:17.798
(Vladimir clearing his throat)

00:00:17.798 --> 00:00:18.631
But in the past few months,

00:00:18.631 --> 00:00:20.654
that image has been challenged.

00:00:20.654 --> 00:00:21.487
(Vladimir clearing his throat)

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.670
Recent footage of the 69-year-old leader

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:24.780
showed him coughing,

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.630
puffy faced or walking
with a stiff right arm,

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.220
fueling speculation and questions

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.570
from the media about his health

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.330
after two years of pandemic isolation.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.160
In late July, intelligence officers

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.510
shared their assessments.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.820
- There's lots of rumors
and as far as we can tell,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.062
he's entirely too healthy.

00:00:41.062 --> 00:00:41.895
(Vladimir clearing his throat)

00:00:41.895 --> 00:00:42.870
- [Narrator] And the
Kremlin has repeatedly said

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.154
he's doing well.

00:00:44.154 --> 00:00:46.440
(Dmitry speaking in foreign language)

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.030
- [Narrator] So amid the war in Ukraine,

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.310
here's why Putin's every public appearance

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.353
is being so closely scrutinized.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.950
First, consider that we're
getting very little information

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.990
from Russia on the president's well-being.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.370
- Good afternoon, everybody.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:00.210
- [Narrator] Unlike the White House

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.700
that shares regular health
updates for US leaders.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.300
- President Biden is currently
experiencing mild symptoms.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.920
- [Narrator] The Kremlin
is very tight lipped

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.004
on the matter.

00:01:09.004 --> 00:01:10.530
(lively music)

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.990
So videos of a seemingly
tired Putin sitting

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.670
at the Victory Day Parade

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.380
or holding the table with both hands

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.989
during this televised update
about the war in Ukraine,

00:01:18.989 --> 00:01:19.830
(Vladimir clearing his throat)

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.300
prompted comments by officials

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.390
and news outlets around the
world about his fitness.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.730
A top Ukrainian official told a TV channel

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.398
that the Russian leader was sick.

00:01:28.398 --> 00:01:32.898
(Kyrylo speaking in foreign language)

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.780
- [Narrator] A Newsweek report claiming

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.340
that American spies believed Putin

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.490
had been treated for
cancer was widely covered.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:47.785
So journalists have been asking
Russian officials about it.

00:01:47.785 --> 00:01:49.368
(journalist speaking in foreign language)

00:01:49.368 --> 00:01:53.868
(Sergei speaking in foreign language)

00:01:59.776 --> 00:02:00.609
(cameras clicking)

00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:01.442
- [Narrator] The Wall Street Journal

00:02:01.442 --> 00:02:03.480
couldn't independently
confirm those reports

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.670
and the leader of a
European country told us

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:08.130
he believed Putin was healthy.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:11.250
Still, observers noticed that
when Putin landed in Tehran,

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.660
he seemed to walk stiffly

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.951
with his right arm hanging unnaturally.

00:02:14.951 --> 00:02:16.380
(Vladimir clearing his throat)

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.730
He also repeated coughed

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.310
and cleared his throat
during and after this trip,

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.014
so much so that he spoke about it himself.

00:02:23.014 --> 00:02:27.681
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.630
- [Narrator] It's obviously
hard to draw any conclusion

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.040
from this type of footage

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.440
but it puts Putin's
health in the spotlight,

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:37.410
even making it a talking point
at a major Security Forum

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:40.590
and prompting Western
intelligence chiefs to weigh in.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:41.670
- There's no evidence

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:46.020
that Putin is suffering
from serious ill health.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:46.853
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:02:46.853 --> 00:02:48.062
- [Narrator] What footage
from the past couple

00:02:48.062 --> 00:02:49.890
of years does show clearly

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.270
is that the Russian leader appears

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.760
to take his physical well-being seriously.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.420
That's what these extremely
long meeting tables suggest.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.860
In the early days of the pandemic,

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.370
Putin went into isolation in
his residence outside Moscow.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.290
During two years, he mostly communicated

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.420
with the outside world via video calls,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.790
like most leaders around the world.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.730
But even after he started
attending more in-person events

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.710
during Russia's war with Ukraine,

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.010
most of the time, the public
has been kept at a distance.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.410
The same goes for
officials and world leaders

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:22.080
who've often been seated
far away from him.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.050
This 16-feet-long table
was seen several times,

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.780
during Putin's meeting with
France's Emmanuel Macron

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.360
and Germany's Olaf Scholz, among others.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.010
The Kremlin said it was keeping in place

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.000
all the safety measures

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.523
to protect the president
from the coronavirus.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:37.620
The health of world leaders

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.750
is always a matter of public concern.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.250
False reports recently claimed

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.420
that the Ukrainian president

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.455
was in intensive care, for example.

00:03:44.455 --> 00:03:46.530
(people cheering)

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.030
But for Russia, heightened scrutiny

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.950
of Putin's health also brings questions

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.720
about how the country would be governed

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.700
without its authoritative leader

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.250
at a time when he's at the
center of global politics

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.710
over the invasion of Ukraine.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.390
For decades, Moscow has worked hard

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.670
to create an aura around one man

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.500
as the country's main decision maker

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.060
who's believed to directly approve

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.493
almost all executive government decisions.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.640
The Kremlin said that Putin's
decision-making powers

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.950
are limited by the Russian constitution,

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.150
and the president's spokesman

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.690
has previously said Moscow
isn't looking for a successor,

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.550
and that means any contingency plan

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:23.251
will likely remain a closely held secret.

00:04:23.251 --> 00:04:25.155
(dramatic music)

